Read a shut lid before connecting outputs

niri connects every output as it starts, in the TTY backend's init,
and hears the lid only afterwards: logind's watcher sends it once the
event loop runs, and libinput's switch events come with the first
input. So a laptop started docked with its lid shut lit its own
panel, laid the monitor out beside it, and took the panel away again
about 70 ms later.

With D-Bus, niri now asks logind whether the lid is shut before the
backend connects anything, so a shut panel is never connected. The
watchers carry on as before; when they report the same, nothing
changes. If logind can't be asked, niri goes on as it did.

diff --git a/src/dbus/freedesktop_login1.rs b/src/dbus/freedesktop_login1.rs
index 5964d45..c945484 100644
--- a/src/dbus/freedesktop_login1.rs
+++ b/src/dbus/freedesktop_login1.rs
@@ -6,6 +6,24 @@ pub enum Login1ToNiri {
     LidClosedChanged(bool),
 }
 
+/// Whether logind says the lid is shut now, asked and answered before niri goes on.
+///
+/// niri connects its outputs as it starts, before the watcher below first reports the lid, so
+/// without this a shut laptop's panel was connected and taken away again a moment later.
+pub fn lid_closed() -> anyhow::Result<bool> {
+    let conn = zbus::blocking::Connection::system()?;
+    let proxy = zbus::blocking::fdo::PropertiesProxy::new(
+        &conn,
+        "org.freedesktop.login1",
+        "/org/freedesktop/login1",
+    )?;
+    let value = proxy.get(
+        InterfaceName::try_from("org.freedesktop.login1.Manager").unwrap(),
+        "LidClosed",
+    )?;
+    Ok(bool::try_from(value)?)
+}
+
 pub fn start(
     to_niri: calloop::channel::Sender<Login1ToNiri>,
 ) -> anyhow::Result<zbus::blocking::Connection> {
diff --git a/src/niri.rs b/src/niri.rs
index 937f1c6..8cfc3be 100644
--- a/src/niri.rs
+++ b/src/niri.rs
@@ -770,6 +770,22 @@ impl State {
             create_wayland_socket,
             is_session_instance,
         );
+
+        // On a screen of its own, niri connects every output as it starts, so a shut lid must be
+        // known first. The watchers report it only once the event loop runs, after the outputs
+        // are connected, so a laptop started shut on a dock lit its panel and laid the monitor
+        // out beside it, to take it away again a moment later.
+        #[cfg(feature = "dbus")]
+        if matches!(backend, Backend::Tty(_)) {
+            match crate::dbus::freedesktop_login1::lid_closed() {
+                Ok(is_closed) => {
+                    debug!("laptop lid {} at start", if is_closed { "closed" } else { "open" });
+                    niri.is_lid_closed = is_closed;
+                }
+                Err(err) => warn!("error reading the lid from login1: {err:?}"),
+            }
+        }
+
         backend.init(&mut niri);
 
         let mut state = Self { backend, niri };
